WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.442
Every meeting spends its attendees' time,

2
00:00:02.442 --> 00:00:04.975
so the first question
is whether to hold one.

3
00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:06.647
Eighteen F's test is simple:

4
00:00:06.647 --> 00:00:10.600
is this meeting a better use of
everyone's time than not meeting?

5
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.572
A faculty-development session
at a children's hospital

6
00:00:13.572 --> 00:00:16.738
in Pittsburgh looked at why
people actually call meetings.

7
00:00:16.738 --> 00:00:20.913
Some reasons are good ones, like giving
information or working a problem.

8
00:00:20.913 --> 00:00:26.088
Others are more honest about habit:
satisfying requirements, or simply tradition.

9
00:00:26.088 --> 00:00:29.924
Its advice is to ask whether some of
those goals could be met another way.

10
00:00:29.924 --> 00:00:33.580
The guide turns that question
into a simple working rule.
